concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6 After subsection 20(2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-6 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (2A) In deciding whether to make a declaration under subsection (1) or (2) in relation to a person and an area, the Minister is limited to considering factors that are relevant to achieving the objects of this Act.  (2B) If an agreement under section 56 or 57 of the Telstra Corporation Act 1991 made between the Commonwealth and a person (including a State or Territory) is expressed to also have effect for the purposes of this subsection, the Minister is taken to have made (and to properly have made) a declaration (the deemed declaration) under subsection (2) that the person is a regional  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime" ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (2A) In deciding whether to make a declaration under subsection (1) or (2) in relation to a person and an area, the Minister is limited to considering factors that are relevant to achieving the objects of this Act.  (2B) If an agreement under section 56 or 57 of the Telstra Corporation Act 1991 made between the Commonwealth and a person (including a State or Territory) is expressed to also have effect for the purposes of this subsection, the Minister is taken to have made (and to properly have made) a declaration (the deemed declaration) under subsection (2) that the person is a regional  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4" ;
