doc:sch-1-sec-24a-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "24A(3) Former universal service provider may be required to provide" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The information that may be required to be given must be information that will assist the current provider in doing something that the current provider is or will be required or permitted to do by or under a provision of this Part. The notice must identify the doing of that thing as the purpose for which the information is required. Note 1: If, for example, information about service location and customer contact details will assist the current provider in fulfilling its obligation under subsection 21(5), the former provider may be required to provide that kind of information. Note 2: See also subsection (5), which allows the Minister to determine that a specified kind of information is information referred to in this subsection." ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24A(4) Former universal service provider may be required to provide"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-24a-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (2) is reasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement as soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the requirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to comply with it.  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If a requirement made by a notice under subsection (2) is reasonable, the former provider must comply with the requirement as soon as practicable after receiving the notice. However, if the requirement is unreasonable, the former provider does not have to comply with it.  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to the universal service regime"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "463364d800f1f140da959960d45e03680a45fff1365409ef97403e830d8e2072" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-24a ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Former universal service provider must comply with reasonable requirements." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
