doc:sch-1-sec-26f-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26F(1) Former digital data service provider may be required to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if:  (a) a person (the former provider) ceases to be a digital data service provider for a particular area (the relevant area) and another person (the current provider) is declared, by declaration that takes effect at the time of that cessation or within the next 6 months, to be a digital data service provider for some or all of that area; or  (b) a person (the former provider) ceases to be a digital data service provider for a particular area (the relevant area) and another person (the current provider) who, before that cessation, was also a digital data service provider for some or all of that area continues after that cessation to be a digital data service provider for some or all of that area. Note: The declaration referred to in paragraph (a) may be a declaration made before, at the same time as, or after the time when the former provider ceases to be a digital data service provider." ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26F(2) Former digital data service provider may be required to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former provider, require the former provider to give to the current provider specified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A notice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:  (a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:  (i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to in paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that declaration takes effect; or  (ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that day; or  (b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former provider ceases to be a digital data service provider for the relevant area.  Amendments relating to the universal service regime  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 1) 2000 No. 95, 2000            13 Note: If paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be given by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that paragraph has not yet taken effect." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former provider, require the former provider to give to the current provider specified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A notice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:  (a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:  (i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to in paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that declaration takes effect; or  (ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that day; or  (b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former provider ceases to be a digital data service provider for the relevant area.  Amendments relating to the universal service regime  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 1) 2000 No. 95, 2000            13 Note: If paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be given by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that paragraph has not yet taken effect."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9a72083a6e3d077d0bef2daaba008aa8aaba23f72a5d219807ce674f91dbc388" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Current provider may require former provider to provide specified information." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
