doc:sch-1-sec-26f-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26F(2) Former digital data service provider may be required to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former provider, require the former provider to give to the current provider specified information of the kind referred to in subsection (3). A notice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:  (a) if paragraph (1)(a) applies:  (i) the later of the day on which the declaration referred to in paragraph (1)(a) was made and the day on which that declaration takes effect; or  (ii) if both of those things happen on the same day—that day; or  (b) if paragraph (1)(b) applies—the day on which the former provider ceases to be a digital data service provider for the relevant area.  Amendments relating to the universal service regime  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 1) 2000 No. 95, 2000            13 Note: If paragraph (1)(a) applies, a notice under this subsection may be given by the current provider even if the declaration referred to in that paragraph has not yet taken effect." ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26F(3) Former digital data service provider may be required to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-26f-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The information that may be required to be given must be information that will assist the current provider in doing something that the current provider is or will be required or permitted to do by or under a provision of this Part. The notice must identify the doing of that thing as the purpose for which the information is required. Note 1: If, for example, information about service location and customer contact details will assist the current provider in fulfilling its obligation under subsection 26B(4) or (5), the former provider may be required to provide that kind of information. Note 2: See also subsection (5), which allows the Minister to determine that a specified kind of information is information referred to in this subsection." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The information that may be required to be given must be information that will assist the current provider in doing something that the current provider is or will be required or permitted to do by or under a provision of this Part. The notice must identify the doing of that thing as the purpose for which the information is required. Note 1: If, for example, information about service location and customer contact details will assist the current provider in fulfilling its obligation under subsection 26B(4) or (5), the former provider may be required to provide that kind of information. Note 2: See also subsection (5), which allows the Minister to determine that a specified kind of information is information referred to in this subsection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b0e9f63f60cd15a90e2a32259a8aa4c8bc1165de07894ae832b195d016d2d257" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-26f ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Current provider must provide information to assist in fulfilling obligations." ;
    dc:description "True" ;
